      en: "Bura Protected Area is a biodiversity reserve in western Yemen, covering dry tropical forests. It hosts wildlife such as the Arabian leopard, baboons, and numerous birds. The area features waterfalls and permanent streams. Flora includes frankincense trees and endemic plants. It is a key watershed and eco-tourism destination. However, deforestation and hunting pose threats.",
